# If you ask me, …
/ɪf juː ˈɑːsk miː/
### jeśli mnie pytasz…, moim zdaniem…
### *A: The new office layout — good idea or not?*
### *B: If you ask me, it's a big improvement.*

# I feel like …
/aɪ ˈfiːl laɪk/
### mam wrażenie, że…, wydaje mi się, że…
### *A: How's the project going?*
### *B: I feel like we're finally making real progress.*

# In my opinion, …
/ɪn maɪ əˈpɪnjən/
### moim zdaniem…
### *A: Which design should we send to the client?*
### *B: In my opinion, the second one is much stronger.*

# To my mind, …
/tə maɪ ˈmaɪnd/
### według mnie…, w moim odczuciu…
### *A: Was the conference worth attending?*
### *B: To my mind, the workshops were the most valuable part.*

# From my point of view, …
/frəm maɪ ˌpɔɪnt əv ˈvjuː/
### z mojego punktu widzenia…
### *A: How does the new schedule look from your side?*
### *B: From my point of view, it's actually easier to plan now.*

# As far as I'm concerned, …
/əz ˌfɑːr əz aɪm kənˈsɜːnd/
### jeśli o mnie chodzi…
### *A: Some people say the meeting was too long.*
### *B: As far as I'm concerned, it could have been an email.*

# Personally, I think …
/ˈpɜːsənəli aɪ ˈθɪŋk/
### osobiście uważam, że…
### *A: Everyone seems to love the new logo.*
### *B: Personally, I think the old one had more character.*

# The way I see it, …
/ðə ˌweɪ ˈaɪ siː ɪt/
### tak jak ja to widzę…
### *A: Why do you think sales dropped last month?*
### *B: The way I see it, we simply raised prices too quickly.*

# I'd say…
/aɪd ˈseɪ/
### powiedziałbym, że…
### *A: How long will the repairs take?*
### *B: I'd say about two weeks, maybe three.*

# If I'm honest, …
/ɪf aɪm ˈɒnɪst/
### jeśli mam być szczery…
### *A: Did you enjoy the film?*
### *B: If I'm honest, I fell asleep halfway through.*

# I'm not sure about that.
/aɪm nɒt ˈʃʊər əˈbaʊt ðæt/
### nie jestem tego pewien
### *A: We could just skip the testing phase to save time.*
### *B: I'm not sure about that — it sounds risky.*

# It depends.
/ɪt dɪˈpendz/
### to zależy
### *A: Is it better to rent or to buy?*
### *B: It depends. How long are you planning to stay?*

# I'm not convinced.
/aɪm nɒt kənˈvɪnst/
### nie jestem przekonany
### *A: This new tool will save us hours every week.*
### *B: I'm not convinced. The last one promised the same thing.*

# I have mixed feelings.
/aɪ hæv ˌmɪkst ˈfiːlɪŋz/
### mam mieszane uczucia
### *A: So, what did you think of the offer?*
### *B: I have mixed feelings. The salary is good, but the commute…*

# That's debatable.
/ðæts dɪˈbeɪtəbl/
### to kwestia dyskusyjna
### *A: Remote teams are always less productive.*
### *B: That's debatable. Ours actually got faster.*

# I wouldn't go that far.
/aɪ ˌwʊdnt gəʊ ˈðæt fɑː/
### nie posunąłbym się tak daleko
### *A: This is the worst decision the company has ever made.*
### *B: I wouldn't go that far. It's a risk, but a calculated one.*

# It's not as simple as that.
/ɪts nɒt əz ˈsɪmpl əz ðæt/
### to nie takie proste
### *A: Why don't we just hire more people?*
### *B: It's not as simple as that — the budget is fixed until April.*

# I disagree.
/ˌaɪ dɪsəˈgriː/
### nie zgadzam się
### *A: I think we should cancel the whole event.*
### *B: I disagree. We've already sold half the tickets.*

# I'm not so sure about that.
/aɪm nɒt ˌsəʊ ˈʃʊər əˈbaʊt ðæt/
### nie byłbym tego taki pewien
### *A: Customers won't notice the price change.*
### *B: I'm not so sure about that. They notice everything.*

# That's not how I see it.
/ðæts ˌnɒt haʊ ˈaɪ siː ɪt/
### ja to widzę inaczej
### *A: You have to admit the project was a failure.*
### *B: That's not how I see it. We learned a lot from it.*

# I see it differently.
/aɪ ˌsiː ɪt ˈdɪfrəntli/
### widzę to inaczej
### *A: The delay was clearly the supplier's fault.*
### *B: I see it differently. Our brief wasn't clear enough.*

# I'm afraid I disagree.
/aɪm əˌfreɪd aɪ dɪsəˈgriː/
### obawiam się, że się nie zgadzam
### *A: I believe this is the best offer we'll get.*
### *B: I'm afraid I disagree. I think we can negotiate further.*

# That doesn't make sense to me.
/ðæt ˌdʌznt meɪk ˈsens tə miː/
### to nie ma dla mnie sensu
### *A: We're cutting the training budget to improve performance.*
### *B: That doesn't make sense to me. How will people improve without training?*

# I can't agree with that.
/aɪ ˌkɑːnt əˈgriː wɪð ðæt/
### nie mogę się z tym zgodzić
### *A: The customer is simply wrong in this case.*
### *B: I can't agree with that. We promised a refund in writing.*

# No way.
/ˌnəʊ ˈweɪ/
### nie ma mowy, w życiu
### *A: Pete says he can finish the report by tonight.*
### *B: No way. It took us three days last time.*

# Not necessarily.
/ˌnɒt ˌnesəˈserəli/
### niekoniecznie
### *A: More meetings mean better communication, right?*
### *B: Not necessarily. Sometimes they just mean less work gets done.*

# I beg to differ.
/aɪ ˌbeg tə ˈdɪfə/
### pozwolę sobie się nie zgodzić
### *A: Surely everyone prefers working from home?*
### *B: I beg to differ. Some of us miss the office.*

# With respect, …
/wɪð rɪˈspekt/
### z całym szacunkiem…
### *A: We've always done it this way.*
### *B: With respect, that doesn't mean it's the best way.*

# I agree.
/ˌaɪ əˈgriː/
### zgadzam się
### *A: I think we should start the meetings on time, no exceptions.*
### *B: I agree. Waiting for latecomers punishes the punctual.*

# I totally agree.
/aɪ ˈtəʊtəli əˈgriː/
### całkowicie się zgadzam
### *A: This café is way better than the one near the office.*
### *B: I totally agree. The coffee actually tastes like coffee.*

# Exactly!
/ɪgˈzæktli/
### dokładnie!, właśnie!
### *A: It's not about working more hours — it's about working smarter.*
### *B: Exactly! That's what I keep saying.*

# I couldn't agree more.
/aɪ ˌkʊdnt əˈgriː mɔː/
### całkowicie się zgadzam, nie mógłbym się bardziej zgodzić
### *A: Good feedback should be honest but kind.*
### *B: I couldn't agree more.*

# That makes sense.
/ˌðæt meɪks ˈsens/
### to ma sens
### *A: We'll test it with a small group before the full launch.*
### *B: That makes sense. Better to find problems early.*

# I see what you mean.
/aɪ ˌsiː wɒt juː ˈmiːn/
### rozumiem, co masz na myśli
### *A: It's not the price — it's the timing that worries me.*
### *B: Ah, I see what you mean. December is a bad month for this.*

# Absolutely.
/ˌæbsəˈluːtli/
### absolutnie, zdecydowanie
### *A: Shall we invite the whole team to the demo?*
### *B: Absolutely. Everyone should see what we've built.*

# Spot on.
/ˌspɒt ˈɒn/
### w punkt, dokładnie tak
### *A: So the real problem is the deadline, not the budget?*
### *B: Spot on. Give us two more weeks and the budget is fine.*

# That's exactly how I see it.
/ðæts ɪgˌzæktli haʊ ˈaɪ siː ɪt/
### dokładnie tak to widzę
### *A: To me, this is an investment, not a cost.*
### *B: That's exactly how I see it.*
